  "question": {
    "text": "The slope of the tangent at any arbitrary point of a curve is twice the product of the abscissa and square of the ordinate of the point. Then, the equation of the curve is&nbsp; (where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi></math> is an arbitrary constant)",
